  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x},$ therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x=-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value of $x.$ \n\n$$\nx=\\text{arcsin}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=-{60}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the required domain. To get a value inside the range, we add ${360}^{\u2218}.$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=x+{360}^{\u2218}=-{60}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}={300}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nSo, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={300}^{\u2218}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={60}^{\u2218}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={60}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978818/assets/5fe064cdc2d97e3db894801f6f31a4679881efcf83564e24a1ea2559c15d2085.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{\u2218}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{\u2218}+{60}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={240}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x={300}^{\u2218},{240}^{\u2218}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=300\\cdot 240=72\\,000.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
